- branch(b1, AND), branch(b2, AND), branch(b3, AND), branch(b4, AND): The source describes a strictly sequential process ("followed by... proceed to... move on to..."), but these nodes hallucinate parallel (AND) splits.
- converge(c1), converge(c2), converge(c3), converge(c4): Hallucinated join points for non-existent concurrent flows, contradicting the linear progression explicitly stated in the source.
- action(n7, "End"): Unwarranted step. The text states "the process comes to an end" as a termination condition, not as a distinct action task; only end(e1) is required.
- precedence(n1, b1), precedence(b1, n2), precedence(n2, b2), precedence(b2, c1), etc.: Insert undocumented split/join nodes between sequential steps, violating SMC3 by disrupting the exact chronology "Start → Pre-admission (T1) → Patient admission (T2) → Detection and treatment (T3) → Discharge (T4) → Follow up (T5) → End".
- actor(a_default, "Default", [i1, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, n6, n7, e1, c1, c2, c3, c4, b1, b2, b3, b4]): The source provides no participant or responsibility information, making this actor declaration and node assignment hallucinated (violates SMC7).